quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  6,74,"When Ibrahim (Abraham) said to his (fostering) father Azar*: ‘Do you take idols for gods? Indeed, I see you and your people in obvious error.’"
  6,75,"Thus did We show Ibrahim (Abraham) the kingdoms of the heavens and the earth, that he might be among the possessors of firm certitude."
  6,76,"So when the night grew dark upon him, he saw a star. He said: ‘This is my Lord!’ But when it set, he said: ‘I do not love things that set.’"
  6,77,"When he saw the moon rising, he said: ‘This is my Lord!’ But when it set, he said: ‘Had my Lord not guided me, I would surely have been among the misguided people.’"
  6,78,"When he saw the sun rising, he said: ‘This must be my Lord! It is bigger (than the other two).’ But when it set, he said: ‘O my people! Indeed, I disown all that you ascribe as (His) partners."
  6,79,"I have turned my face towards the One Who has originated the heavens and the earth, being an upright believer, and I am not among the polytheists.’"
  6,80,"His people argued with him. He said: ‘Do you argue with me concerning Allah while He has guided me? I do not fear whatever (idols) you ascribe to Him (as His) partners, except anything that my Lord may wish. My Lord comprehends all things in (His) knowledge. Will you then not remember?"
  6,81,"How should I fear the partners you ascribe when you do not fear ascribing partners to Allah, for which He has not sent down any authority to you? So which of the two parties has a greater right to safety if (only) you know?’"
